{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"00a9f3fa758d50c649ea78c77989de5a059306e9"},"timestamp":1557852727,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NDQwMjE2NzQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3404","origin":"github"},"title":"Request: Respect NO_COLOR environment variable","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nThere is no obvious way to disable ANSI colors in the terminal outputs. There is an effort to have CLI tools uniformly respect a `NO_COLOR` environment variable, which seems like a good place to start. See https://no-color.org/.\n\nThe context this comes up in is in [this example notebook](https://fitlins.readthedocs.io/en/latest/examples/ds003_sample_analysis.html#install-data-and-fitlins), where Sphinx does not properly render ANSI colors. It would be useful to simply disable them at the datalad end, rather than play around on the parsing end.\n\n[snipped other headers]","files":null}]}